From 4df24345b528d051873abf775139f41469c94d25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:26:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: re-pin the MSL/DWC tool profiles and correct the gate
 path (1602)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three more decomp build tools pin their inputs: tools/msl-new-partition,
tools/msl-d1-partition and tools/dwc-iterator-advance. Patch 1601 only
re-pinned the two alarm-partition profiles, so the DS gate stops with
"header drift" at lib/include/nitro/types.h and then "unregistered source"
at the MSL operator-new partitions.

Inputs changed since the pins were recorded:

- lib/include/nitro/types.h — patch 1001 (u64/s64 aligned(4), inside
  SDK_PORT_3DS; the Metrowerks text is unchanged).
- lib/NitroDWC/src/tree-iterator4.h — the pinned upstream commit itself
  (8cbb4a1); the profile still carried the previous commit's hash.
- src/to91_msl_{scalar,array}_new.cpp — patches 1505 (drop the dynamic
  exception specifications) and 1519 (operator new's first parameter is
  __SIZE_TYPE__) under SDK_PORT_3DS; msl-new-partition pins the producer
  sources by SHA-256 as well as the headers.

Only recorded hashes change. The DS build is unchanged, which the ROM SHA1
gate proves.

The gate procedure also changes: clone the patched tree to
/work/pokeheartgold, not /work/patched. The MSL partition tools pin the
complete producer object and MWCC embeds the absolute source directory, so
a build from any other path fails with "complete producer
section/symbol/relocation/payload drift" even though the code is
identical. docs/wiki/Daily-Workflow.md and docs/progress/phase-1.md now
say so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
